{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/839740-translating-the-translations-2e-updates-for-wod-translation-guides","id":839740,"title":"Translating the Translations: 2e Updates for WoD Translation Guides","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T00:58:44-08:00","id":839740,"title":"Translating the Translations: 2e Updates for WoD Translation Guides","content":"First of all, I'm really sorry if this has already been handled elsewhere, so mods, please redirect me and lock this <br /> <br /> So, we're all quite familiar with the fact that fans of either version of the World of Darkness often have things that they like in the other version as well. So much so that Onyx Path Publishing created the WoD Translation Guides, with official crunch for converting various titbits from one system to its setting approximate in the other. And there was much rejoicing and complaining with equal vehemence.<br /> <br /> Only problem is, with the transition from Worlds of Darkness Old and New to World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness, three of the four Translation Guides are now obsolete, working on rules and even some minor setting assumptions about the New World of Darkness that are no longer true.<br /> <br /> Now, I figure that OPP will put out 2e revisions on their own accord, eventually. But that's little help to me now, especially since I damn well stink at mechanical homebrewing.<br /> <br /> So, I opened this topic with the hope that more adept crunchcrafters would be willing to share their thoughts, opinions and other forms of expertise when it comes to mechanically updating at least the Vampire and Werewolf Translation Guides?<br /> <br /> Since my own download abilities are, to put it mildly, atrocious, I've only been able to read the WTG thus far. So, I was wondering if folks could advise me on how to translate the Ragabash and Philodox auspices and the Ulle'u and Urhanu (Forsaken equivalents to Metis and Lupus) breeds/origins to the 2nd edition of Werewolf the Forsaken?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that directly stating the material from the guides is forbidden, but I think I'm allowed to make references, like &quot;Urhana are biased away from Mental stats in terms of primacy, suffer stronger penalties when using Mental checks untrained, have much higher starting Harmony and have an easier time stepping between worlds&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T07:33:10-08:00","id":839883,"title":"","content":"Stew actually did an official-ish update of Urhanu on <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">the blog</a> a while back. (scroll down a bit, it's just under the Boys N the Hood poster) <br /> <br /> There's no such update for metis equivalents, because 2e as a whole kind of ditched the whole &quot;spiritual incest&quot; concept entirely. I guess you could have a werewolf who's basically in The Father's Form by default or something though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T09:58:17-08:00","id":839988,"title":"","content":"Thanks for pointing me in that direction. Hmm... I know that 2e did drop that angle, still, I do wonder if the Ulle'u could be adapted to 2e...<br /> <br /> What about the Auspices? Any pointers on fixing them up under the conversion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:22:10-08:00","id":840143,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken\">I'm working on that right now.</a> (No, that's not a coincidence.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  fixed link 03-01-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:41:19-07:00","id":965191,"title":"","content":"So, Dataweaver's thread is all about the Ulle'u and Urhanu getting a shiny new 2e update, but, as I asked, I was wondering if anyone has any thoughts on adapting the Ragabash and the Philodox to 2e Forsaken?<br /> <br /> Likewise, what about upgrading the Translation Guides for Vampire &amp; Mage now that both of those games have 2e versions to compare them too?<br /> <br /> Also, on the &quot;extra Auspices&quot;, do you think it's fair to rule that Ragabashs are guaranteed to experience the First Change under a lunar eclipse, but they may also randomly occur when a new werewolf changes under a new or waning moon? It's just that A: Philodoxes are encouraged to &quot;share&quot; the Half-Moon with Elodoths, and B: to my understanding, lunar eclipses are rare, so that'd make a Ragabash almost &quot;last of the White Walkers&quot; tier special snowflake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:26:28-07:00","id":965230,"title":"","content":"Check out the stuff linked in my signature, in regards to Vampire, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-for